  "text": "Let the studio drive itself with rules, macros and hardware controllers — every one of them limited to one fixed list of studio commands, so no automation can name a file, start a program or reach the internet. Rules, macros and variables Open Tools → Automation Rules & Macros… and add a rule. Pick one of nine triggers (a scene switch, the stream starting or stopping, the recording starting or stopping, a source error, an audio level crossing a line, the system going idle, a window taking focus, a time of day, or a watched file changing), add conditions (a variable's value, live, recording), and choose a studio action. Every rule starts disabled : turn it on to arm it. Build a macro as a named list of steps — run an action, wait, set a variable — with a repeat count and an optional global hotkey. Run it from the app, a hotkey, a rule or the remote-control API. Set a studio variable in a macro and use it as {{name}} inside any Text source: the text changes the moment the macro sets the value. Controllers: MIDI, OSC and the touch panel Open Tools → MIDI Control… and teach it a pad, knob or fader for an action, a macro, a scene switch, a mixer fader or a mute — with lights and motoriz"
