  "heading": "Virtual camera",
  "text": "Use your program as a webcam in any video-call app. Windows only in 1.2.1. Click Start Virtual Camera in Controls . Freally Capture adds a system camera called \"Freally Capture Virtual Camera\" . In Zoom, Meet, Discord or Teams, choose that camera in the video settings: your program becomes the webcam. Click Stop Virtual Camera to remove it. Per system: on Windows the camera registers for your user, with no administrator rights, and is removed when you stop it. It is not yet code-signed , so Windows may warn about it and a hardened video-call app may refuse it; a full test inside a live call is still to be done. The macOS and Linux cameras are separate components that are not in this release . Freally Capture never installs a system component without asking, on any system."
