  "text": "A smooth-scrolling script for the person on camera — on a panel in the app, a fullscreen projector that can be mirrored, and the LAN touch panel, all at once. Open the teleprompter from Tools , type or paste your script, and set the speed and font. Pace it in characters per second , or switch to BPM (50–250 beats per minute) to read lyrics in time with music; either change re-paces a running scroll. Pause chips: type -- for a beat or --N for an N-second hold and it becomes a single chip — the cursor steps over it, one Delete or Backspace removes it, and copy and paste keep it whole. Start countdown: arm an optional 3-2-1 lead-in, shown on both the operator's preview and the projector, so the reader has a beat before the text moves. Open the projector for the reader (mirror mode flips it for beam-splitter glass). Opening it closes the operator window, so you can run the stream from the main window while they read; with a countdown armed, the projector goes back to the top, counts down and plays. Play, pause, stop, rewind, fast-forward and restart from the on-screen controls, a hotkey, MIDI, OSC or the LAN panel — every control stays in step. Read aloud previews the script with your "
